# Byte identity is the point: the launcher and its peers compare SHA-256 hashes
# of the pack's files, so git must not touch a single byte - no line-ending
# conversion, no filters.
#
# This arrived late. core.autocrlf is true system-wide on the machine this pack
# was laid out on, so 753 of its text files went into git with their CRLFs
# stripped and have differed from the copy on disk ever since. What players
# have is the git copy - the runner that builds the release checks out exactly
# these bytes - so the divergence was resolved in git's favour rather than the
# other way round, and no file any player holds changed.
* -text
